      {
        "id": 175349,
        "name": "deddragon",
        "username": "deddragon",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/deddragon/{size}/2335_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-05-06T00:58:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Managed to get Mint, but I really shouldn’t have!<br>\nI knew when I saw it was this team that I should have done some big card draw but I decided to go another route. I left the ship and Targeting Innocents out and applied shenanigans with a first round Smoke Bombs to both mitigate damage and direct as much flame as possible to Absolute Zero who had used his Transducer.  On round two AZ placed and used Coolant Blast to destroy the ship, and unfortunately that was about the sum of his damage-dealing. Soon after, he seemed to forget about the Cramped Quarters and punched himself to death.<br>\nThe rest of the game went like so:<br>\nTempest killed one or two things per turn and used Cleansing Downpour. Never used his innate power once.  He saved Into the Stratosphere for the Forced Deployments so only one of those actually went off.<br>\nWraith focused on damage, using Throwing Knives and Razor Ordinance every turn. When Tempest put the first Forced Deployment back, Wraith used the Eyepiece (one turn too late, because the other top card was also Forced Deployment.)<br>\nTachy Sucker-Punched those pesky Soldiers that were immune to projectile and threw cards at everyone. She also shut down damage twice, and very timely.<br>\nBunker dealt and soaked damage. A lot of damage. No Omni-cannon for me, but Turret Mode with Flak Cannon + Grenade Launcher with the occasional Maintenance.<br>\nIncapsolute Zero shut down the environment because that’s what he does.<br>\nWith the final card (the first Forced Deployment back for a third time) of Voss’s deck imminent and everyone under 5hp Bunker and Tempest cleared the table so Wraith could sacrifice her tech and Tachion could double Barrage for 49 points between them.</p>\n<p>And right before that the game glitched (see attached.)  It’s actually the second time I saw this happen in a game, and on that character’s turn they didn’t actually have the card. Fun though <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=9\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"></p>",
        "post_number": 23,
