      {
        "id": 175350,
        "name": "robb8888",
        "username": "robb8888",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-05-06T07:03:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"jffdougan\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/48/1882_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jffdougan:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Cuthawolf wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Bleh. That was the black hole from which Fun did not escape. Gonna pass on these one-shots for a while, they just make me feel stupid.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nI dunno if it makes you feel any better, but Advanced Voss and Advanced Dawn are in the half-dozen hardest fights in the game.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>…and the villain/environment deck were stacked to make the fight harder than it should have been. &nbsp;Two Hostage Situations in the first five rounds? &nbsp;C'mon! &nbsp;I played this same scenario as a custom game (i.e. picking Advanced Voss/Freedom Five/Megalopolis) five times after finishing the one-shot, and wiped the floor with Advanced Voss every time. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>AZ is the key–once he has his two modules, you make sure he's the highest HP hero, then kill all of the minions except the one that does 2 fire damage to the highest HP hero. &nbsp;Now you're essentially immune to damage from Voss, because the minion will whack AZ for 2 fire damage…which AZ will redirect into cold damage aimed at himself, thus healing himself from the fire damage. &nbsp;From that point, you're free to build your hands/setups (using the insane amounts of card draw these heroes have) and kill Voss at your leisure.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:58:54.823Z",
