      {
        "id": 175353,
        "name": "The Burning Stickman",
        "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-05-07T01:29:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mint, and definitely a slow-burn game. Voss was down to 5 cards in his deck by the time I was finished, Wraith's deck and trash were both empty and my computer nearly froze when I was picking out which cards to load the Omni-Cannon with. Absolute Zero was MVP, as I'm getting is expected with this one, and this is the first game I got real mileage out of Coolant Blast.</p><p>I actually really liked having a long game -- most games I have are over quick enough that AZ only manages to get out his basic equipment, and it was nice to have more of his stuff out for longer.</p><p>Both the Forced Deployments I saw came out with Voss flipped, which made them easy to deal with (one set fell to Grappling Hook, Razor Ordnance to deal with the Gene-Bound Guard, and a Sonic Vortex to wipe out everyone else; the second went down to a Fueled Freeze, with a pair of Synaptic Interruptions going down to boost it to 3+Focused Apertures).</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:58:55.040Z",
